{
  "id": "CJm4W_7MB4Y",
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.04,
      "end": 5.32,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "We had a small issue today.",
          "start": 0.04,
          "end": 1.68
        },
        {
          "text": "One of the boys, Patrick, said Lily, pushed him down and tried to kiss him.",
          "start": 1.72,
          "end": 5.32
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 5.56,
      "end": 11.16,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "No, that doesn't sound like Lily.",
          "start": 5.56,
          "end": 7.32
        },
        {
          "text": "She was probably imitating something she saw on TV or in her family.",
          "start": 7.36,
          "end": 11.16
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "imitate",
          "ko": "흉내 내다, 따라 하다",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.2,
      "end": 15.24,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "It was the TV, yes.",
          "start": 11.2,
          "end": 12.45
        },
        {
          "text": "Here she is. She's always so sweet.",
          "start": 13.01,
          "end": 15.24
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 15.84,
      "end": 19.52,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Bye, Patrick.",
          "start": 15.84,
          "end": 17.26
        },
        {
          "text": "See? They're just friends.",
          "start": 17.26,
          "end": 19.52
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 19.96,
      "end": 22.72,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "What are you laughing at, Evan?",
          "start": 19.96,
          "end": 21.52
        },
        {
          "text": "You're next.",
          "start": 21.56,
          "end": 22.72
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 24.16,
      "end": 31.2,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Okay, I'm going to talk to her for a little bit.",
          "start": 24.16,
          "end": 26.04
        },
        {
          "text": "Oh, did I ever tell you that I put your name up here?",
          "start": 28.48,
          "end": 31.2
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 32.64,
      "end": 36.4,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Haley Dunphy Dome.",
          "start": 32.64,
          "end": 34.2
        },
        {
          "text": "Oh, you named her special spots?",
          "start": 34.28,
          "end": 36.4
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "spacing",
          "ko": "(글자) 띄어쓰기, 간격",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 36.44,
      "end": 40.8,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Actually, it was supposed to be Haley Dunphy do me.",
          "start": 36.44,
          "end": 39.47
        },
        {
          "text": "I'm bad with spacing.",
          "start": 39.47,
          "end": 40.8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 41.52,
      "end": 43.48,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Oh.",
          "start": 41.52,
          "end": 42.02
        },
        {
          "text": "You're not so bad.",
          "start": 42.48,
          "end": 43.48
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 44.44,
      "end": 51.6,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "And that's halftime. Panthers six, Dolphins zero.",
          "start": 44.44,
          "end": 47.68
        },
        {
          "text": "That's zero scored by Jason Miller, who proudly prances off the field.",
          "start": 47.8,
          "end": 51.6
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "halftime",
          "ko": "(경기) 하프타임, 전반 종료",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "prance off",
          "ko": "의기양양하게 걸어 나가다",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 51.84,
      "end": 55.91,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Just let me go up there and kick that kid's butt.",
          "start": 51.84,
          "end": 53.7
        },
        {
          "text": "Knock it off, Miller. I need your leg. Take a knee.",
          "start": 53.7,
          "end": 55.91
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "Knock it off",
          "ko": "그만해, 작작 해",
          "type": "idiom"
        },
        {
          "term": "Take a knee",
          "ko": "무릎 꿇고 모여 (작전 지시)",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 56.51,
      "end": 63.04,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Now. I don't know what tuna net you dolphins swam into, but you are drowning out there.",
          "start": 56.51,
          "end": 60.52
        },
        {
          "text": "Coach, would it really be such a bad thing if we lost?",
          "start": 60.56,
          "end": 63.04
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "drowning out there",
          "ko": "(경기에서) 허우적대다, 헤매다",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 63.08,
      "end": 66.6,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Beg your pardon?",
          "start": 63.08,
          "end": 63.92
        },
        {
          "text": "Look at them, coach. Haven't they lost enough already?",
          "start": 64.08,
          "end": 66.6
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "Beg your pardon?",
          "ko": "뭐라고요? (정중한 되물음)",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 66.8,
      "end": 71.28,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Maybe giving them a win would, in a way, be a victory for us too.",
          "start": 66.8,
          "end": 69.84
        },
        {
          "text": "Okay, you know what mattered the most to Coach Knight?",
          "start": 69.84,
          "end": 71.28
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "in a way",
          "ko": "어떤 면에서는",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 71.32,
      "end": 74.71,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "His work with special needs kids?",
          "start": 71.32,
          "end": 72.64
        },
        {
          "text": "Okay. He took one kid to one beach, one time.",
          "start": 72.64,
          "end": 74.71
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 74.71,
      "end": 79.08,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Football.",
          "start": 74.71,
          "end": 75.68
        },
        {
          "text": "Football is what mattered the most. He lived for competition.",
          "start": 75.88,
          "end": 79.08
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "lived for competition",
          "ko": "경쟁에 살았다, 경쟁이 낙이었다",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "sportsmanship",
          "ko": "스포츠맨십, 정정당당함",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 79.12,
      "end": 89.6,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "He believed in sportsmanship, integrity.",
          "start": 79.12,
          "end": 82.32
        },
        {
          "text": "Okay, now, the way I see it, we can roll over and give them an empty, meaningless victory that he would hate.",
          "start": 83.08,
          "end": 89.6
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "integrity",
          "ko": "진실성, 올곧음",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "roll over",
          "ko": "(싸우지 않고) 순순히 져 주다",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 89.8,
      "end": 99.6,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Or we can go out there, leave it all on the field and be a team he would be proud to lose to.",
          "start": 89.8,
          "end": 96.04
        },
        {
          "text": "Now, is this an I activity or a we activity?",
          "start": 97.28,
          "end": 99.6
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "leave it all on the field",
          "ko": "(경기에) 모든 걸 쏟아붓다",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 99.64,
      "end": 100.82,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "We!",
          "start": 99.64,
          "end": 100.2
        },
        {
          "text": "What?",
          "start": 100.2,
          "end": 100.82
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 100.82,
      "end": 103.25,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "We! - What?",
          "start": 100.82,
          "end": 101.68
        },
        {
          "text": "We! We! We! We!",
          "start": 101.68,
          "end": 103.25
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 103.25,
      "end": 108.55,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "That's right. Now you sound like dolphins!",
          "start": 103.25,
          "end": 106.52
        },
        {
          "text": "Hey, Tim.",
          "start": 107.32,
          "end": 108.55
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 108.55,
      "end": 113.12,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Got the next three days of delivery slips for you here signed, huh.",
          "start": 108.55,
          "end": 112.38
        },
        {
          "text": "Thanks, Claire.",
          "start": 112.38,
          "end": 113.12
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "delivery slips",
          "ko": "배송 전표",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 113.2,
      "end": 116.45,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Yeah. Sign those up. Good, huh?",
          "start": 113.2,
          "end": 115.12
        },
        {
          "text": "Yup. Mhm. - Yeah.",
          "start": 115.16,
          "end": 116.45
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 116.45,
      "end": 120.12,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Yeah, thanks.",
          "start": 116.45,
          "end": 117.25
        },
        {
          "text": "So this is this is the, uh, the Regency. Birch.",
          "start": 117.25,
          "end": 120.12
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 120.16,
      "end": 124.04,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Beautiful model. Gorgeous.",
          "start": 120.16,
          "end": 121.96
        },
        {
          "text": "You guys do such good work down here.",
          "start": 121.96,
          "end": 124.04
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 124.16,
      "end": 128.32,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Really, you mind if I take her for a spin before she goes up to the showroom?",
          "start": 124.16,
          "end": 127.4
        },
        {
          "text": "You're the boss.",
          "start": 127.4,
          "end": 128.32
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "take her for a spin",
          "ko": "(차 등을) 한번 몰아 보다, 시운전하다",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 128.32,
      "end": 131.36,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "His daughter.",
          "start": 128.32,
          "end": 129.56
        },
        {
          "text": "Yeah. That's what you want to say.",
          "start": 129.92,
          "end": 131.36
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 131.72,
      "end": 138.49,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Oh, okay. So. So no mirror when they're shipping, which makes sense.",
          "start": 131.72,
          "end": 135.4
        },
        {
          "text": "Also have a...",
          "start": 137.36,
          "end": 138.49
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 139.35,
      "end": 143.18,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "No handles.",
          "start": 139.35,
          "end": 140.8
        },
        {
          "text": "Hey. Hey, Tim.",
          "start": 141.76,
          "end": 143.18
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 145.02,
      "end": 149.45,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Hey, Tim?",
          "start": 145.02,
          "end": 147.23
        },
        {
          "text": "Tim!",
          "start": 147.35,
          "end": 149.45
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 149.97,
      "end": 155.01,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Oh, God. Yeah. Hi, dad.",
          "start": 149.97,
          "end": 152.17
        },
        {
          "text": "Hey, coworker. Just seeing when you want to leave for the game.",
          "start": 152.21,
          "end": 155.01
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 155.05,
      "end": 157.77,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "We're late already.",
          "start": 155.05,
          "end": 156.29
        },
        {
          "text": "Soon. Soon.",
          "start": 156.33,
          "end": 157.77
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 159.19,
      "end": 164.93,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "I'm just. I'm finishing up a little paperwork in my office.",
          "start": 159.19,
          "end": 162.55
        },
        {
          "text": "Okay. Let me know if you need any help.",
          "start": 162.55,
          "end": 164.93
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 164.97,
      "end": 168.41,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "No, I do not need your help.",
          "start": 164.97,
          "end": 166.09
        },
        {
          "text": "And as I believe I mentioned.",
          "start": 166.09,
          "end": 168.41
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "look over my shoulder",
          "ko": "(어깨너머로) 감시하다, 간섭하다",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 168.45,
      "end": 176.41,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "I would appreciate it if you were not constantly looking over my shoulder.",
          "start": 168.45,
          "end": 173.77
        },
        {
          "text": "Come on, give me some credit. That's the last thing I would do.",
          "start": 173.81,
          "end": 176.41
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "give me some credit",
          "ko": "나 좀 믿어 줘, 그 정도는 인정해 줘",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 176.45,
      "end": 185.93,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Dad, you seem to forget that I raised three children and I had a career before this.",
          "start": 176.45,
          "end": 183.49
        },
        {
          "text": "I have done plenty of stuff that does not.",
          "start": 183.53,
          "end": 185.93
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 186.09,
      "end": 191.49,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Oh!",
          "start": 186.09,
          "end": 186.59
        },
        {
          "text": "Do you hear that? Sounds like it's coming from the warehouse.",
          "start": 188.33,
          "end": 191.49
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 191.61,
      "end": 193.01,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Yeah.",
          "start": 191.61,
          "end": 191.97
        },
        {
          "text": "What even is that?",
          "start": 191.97,
          "end": 193.01
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 194.93,
      "end": 199.73,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Oh, I'm sure it's nothing.",
          "start": 194.93,
          "end": 196.41
        },
        {
          "text": "Uh, one piece of advice. Take it or leave it.",
          "start": 196.89,
          "end": 199.73
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "Take it or leave it",
          "ko": "받아들이든 말든 (양자택일)",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 201.05,
      "end": 204.65,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "What?",
          "start": 201.05,
          "end": 201.61
        },
        {
          "text": "The latch is under the panel on the right.",
          "start": 202.01,
          "end": 204.65
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "latch",
          "ko": "걸쇠, 빗장",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
